      ":question/id": "3dea8fb2-6f73-566b-a667-5c1dd38bc42a",
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $1$st column.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
